== Tips ==
*The '''Enderman Pet''' is a useful pet for early game, due to its cheap [[Auction House]] price and relatively common drop rate. It provides great damage for people who can't spend a lot of money or are [[Ironman]].
**The {{Uncommon}} rarity does not provide a higher damage buff, therefore it may be better to get a {{Common}} pet, as it levels faster, unless the player wants the {{Rare}}, {{Legendary}}, or {{Mythic}} perks.
**While {{AN|Teleport Savvy}} no longer applies when swapping pets, the ability still grants a significant damage bonus while the pet is active.
*It is recommended to sell non-{{Rarity|l}} or {{Rarity|m}} '''Enderman Pets''' to {{NPCSprite|George}} as they sell for a very low amount on the [[Auction House]] due to how many Enderman Pets are in circulation.

== Trivia ==
* The {{Rarity|m}} '''Enderman Pet''' is one of {{Green|5}} pets designed for its respective [[Slayer]]: the others being the {{Item|Ghoul Pet}} for [[Zombie Slayer]], the {{Item|Tarantula Pet}} for [[Spider Slayer]], the {{Rarity|m}} {{Item|Hound Pet}} for [[Wolf Slayer]], and the {{Item|Wisp Pet}} for [[Blaze Slayer]].
*The {{AN|Teleport Savvy}} ability buffs the {{Stat|dmg}} of all weapons with a teleportation ability (e.g. {{Item|Sinseeker Scythe}}, {{Item|Necron's Blade}}{{Confirm}}, etc) and is not limited to the {{Item|Aspect of the End}} or {{Item|Aspect of the Void}}.
*The '''Enderman Pet''' used to be swapped to for the {{AN|Teleport Savvy}} ability bonus, before being swapped out with pet rules. This behavior has since been patched.
*The first [[Pet Skins|pet skin]] in the game, the [[Spooky Enderman Skin]], is an '''Enderman Pet''' skin.

